Purpose: the hooks of tools/qjs2c, the ZN-599 spike that compiles QuickJS bytecode functions to C. Under #ifdef ZN_QJS_AOT (CMake
  -DZN_QJS_AOT_GEN=<generated file>): JSFunctionBytecode holds the compiled body and its atom table, JS_CallInternal runs a bound body in
  the frame it set up (an exception goes back to the interpreter, which unwinds and resumes interpreting at a catch), and
  zn_qjs_aot_bind matches the generated table at the first call (file, line, column, bytes with atom operands masked). Under
  ZN_QJS_PROFILE: JS_ZnProfBytecode gives the code and stack size for the dumps qjs2c reads.
Measured: decision no-go, D55 (docs/reports/zinc-next-qjs2c.md): 1.08-1.40x on the four workloads of the report, code 53-61x the
  bytecode; the QuickJS T1 programs and the test262 regexp subset give the same results with every function compiled. Off by default:
  quickjs.c compiled with zn_quickjs's flags (-O2) gives the same instructions as the release (otool -tv).
Upstream: not upstreamable: a Zinc-specific spike interface.
